# 076.RecAFilament -- protein and DNA in one system

Four RecA protomers of a nucleoprotein filament with the dT13 strand they
wrap, all-atom, under the full bonded model.

    make prep     build reca.nc
    make point    the energy table below
    make run      dynamics, drivable from VMD or UnityMol


## What it is for

074 and 075 exercise nucleic acids alone; 070-073 exercise proteins alone.
This is the only example where BOTH parameter sets are loaded at once, and
that is the thing it tests.

pdb2spn takes one --grp and one --nonbondedinteraction, so the Makefile
concatenates them. That works only because the type names cannot collide:
amber.grp prefixes every protein type with an UPPERCASE residue letter (ACA
for ALA's CA) while amber.dna.grp uses lowercase and digits (dC5, 1C1).
amber.dna.grp was built that way deliberately, for this case; before this
example, nothing had ever checked it. The rigid-body and bonded rules
concatenate too, their residue sets being disjoint.


## The system, and what was done to it

3CMX is the RecA-DNA filament this example's system comes from -- the same
structure the coarse-grained example 022.RecA uses, at all-atom resolution
here, which makes this a different model of the same object rather than a
reproduction of it.

Kept: the four RecA protomers whose backbone is continuous in the crystal
(chain A residues 37-333, 1001-1333, 2001-2333, 3001-3333, split into four
chains here since they are four molecules) and the dT13 strand. 10020 heavy
atoms in, about 20000 once hydrogenated.

Dropped, and why:

  * ADP, Mg and AlF4. No AMBER template, and no parameters of ours either --
    modelling them would be a separate piece of work, not a preparation
    step.
  * the fifth protomer. Residues 4155-4167 and 4197-4204 are disordered and
    absent from the crystal, and rebuilding 21 residues of backbone is a
    modelling decision. It is also the protomer that touches the DNA least
    -- 153 atom pairs within 5 A, against 264 to 373 for the other four
    (measured, not assumed).
  * the strand's free 5'-monophosphate, leaving a 5'-OH. AMBER has no
    template for it and it is what tleap builds from a sequence.

Added: the terminal OXT of each protein chain, by pdbfixer. It reports no
missing side-chain atom anywhere, which is worth knowing -- a missing heavy
atom is not a warning but a template error deep inside createSystem.

Then minimised and run 5 ps at 300 K with GBn2 implicit solvent, like every
other structure in these examples. A crystal is cold, packed and away from
the force field's own equilibrium; it is never used as deposited.


## Stiffness, deliberately 250 and not 3000

074.DNADuplex runs at 3000 kJ/mol/A^2 because the furanose rings carry no
bonded rule of their own and are held by the mesh alone. Here the value is
250, the protein examples' validated one, so those rings relax more than
they do in 074.

That is the right trade for this example: raising the stiffness for 13
nucleotides would stiffen 1188 protein residues with them, and the pucker
is already measured properly in 074 and 075. What this example is about is
the two chemistries coexisting.
